[Music]  every year science chooses one fantastic  discovery as its breakthrough of the  year  before we get to it here are a few of  the runners up  [Music]  dna from fossils has transformed what we  know about evolution  now scientists are digging up dna from  an entirely different place  the soil itself  in spain dna extracted from a cave floor  revealed that three groups of  neanderthals had once occupied it and  only one remained at the end of the last  ice age  in a cave in the country of georgia  scientists found a female genome from a  previously unknown line of neanderthals  and in another cave in northern mexico  twelve thousand-year-old dna from four  black bears revealed that their  descendants migrated to alaska as the  climate warmed  new techniques that sift nuclear dna  from ancient soil made these findings  possible as the method spreads expect  many more answers to questions about  earth's ancient past  nasa's insight spacecraft is bringing  the interior of mars into focus like  never before  soon after its 2018 arrival the lander  detected a handful of mars quakes these  underground tremors revealed that the  thin martian crust has at least two  layers maybe as many as three  that thin shell would have made it easy  for the planet to shed heat early in its  history  one layer down mars mantle is also  thinner than expected lacking an  insulating lower half at the planet's  center is a huge liquid nickel iron core  but insight is running out of time it  has just a few months to hear more  quakes before martian dust covers its  solar panels and it powers down forever  in 2021 psychedelic drugs got a big  boost in mainstream medicine one major  study found that patients with  post-traumatic stress disorder improved  so much on the drug mdma and talk  therapy that two-thirds no longer had  the disorder after two months  the results brought excitement and  caution  nearly all participants correctly  guessed that they had received the drug  rather than the placebo perhaps due to  its psychoactive effects that might have  enhanced their expectations and their  odds of improving still if another  ongoing study can confirm these results  the treatment may be up for approval by  the u.s food and drug administration as  early as 2023  a new weapon is joining the fight  against covid19  anti-viral pills that can prevent  symptoms and death if taken early enough  this fall drug makers pfizer and merck  released clinical trial results still  under peer review that hinted at early  success  merck's antiviral reduced the risk of  hospitalization or death by 30 percent  in high unvaccinated individuals  meanwhile pfizer's two-drug approach  reduced hospitalization by 89  in the same group  there are concerns that the results may  not be as good as they appear and that  off-target effects in merck's pill could  cause troublesome mutations  the pills are also no replacement for a  vaccine  but if they become widely available they  could reduce death blunt breakthrough  infections and even cut transmission of  sars kovi 2 worldwide  and now the breakthrough of the year  for more than 50 years scientists have  tried to understand how proteins the  building blocks of biology transform  from simple chains of amino acids into  precisely folded 3d structures those  structures determine how proteins  interact with other molecules and could  reveal everything from unknown drug  targets to new insights into basic  biology  this year the power of artificial  intelligence improved those predictions  by magnitudes  before ai entered the scene scientists  used experimental techniques to map  proteins atom by atom researchers have  used these methods to uncover the  structures of more than 180 000 proteins  but such work is slow and expensive  to speed things up scientists started  using computers to predict the shapes  that proteins might take for the last  two decades those predictions have  gotten better but they still have room  for improvement  then ai changed everything alpha fold a  program developed by google's sister  company deepmind outshone every team at  a major competition in 2018  and in 2020 alpha fold 2 showed that it  could predict proteins as well as  experimental techniques a major  milestone and this year researchers at  deepmind solved  350 000 human protein structures 44 of  all known human proteins and a really  good fraction of the 200 million thought  to exist  other researchers are using ai to  predict how proteins come together and  interact for a wide variety of  applications even now alpha fold 2 is  modeling the spike protein in the new  omicron variant of sars cov2 and  scientists are eagerly awaiting results  [Music]  you

